<title>NORWAY: Aker RGI shipyard wins Japanese contract.</title>
<headline>Aker RGI shipyard wins Japanese contract.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brattvaag Skipsverft AS, a partly-owned subsidiary of Norwegian industrial holding company Aker RGI, said on Monday it had won a contract to deliver two supply boat vesssels from The Sanko Steamship Co in Tokyo, Japan.</p>
<p>The contract was valued at 230 million crowns.  </p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
